     "<div>Hi all,</div><div><br></div><div>Not sure if my message got posted so here it is again, just in case. I am running simulations of data to evaluate the sensitivity of removal count models to varying abundance and detection probability and so far everything was going more or less ok. However, when I tried to obtain posterior estimates for abundance <i>ranef </i>produced the error:</div><div><br></div><div>Error in matrix(NA, M, J) : non-numeric matrix extent</div><div><br></div><div>Here is an example of the data and models produced:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><br><span><span><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><font size=\"1\">&gt;summary(data$ab_140_det_0.1725)</font></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span><font size=\"1\">unmarkedFrame Object<br><br>1 sites<br>Maximum number of observations per site: 32 <br>Mean number of observations per site: 32 <br>Number of primary survey periods: 1 <br>Number of secondary survey periods: 32 <br>Sites with at least one detection: 1 <br><br>Tabulation of y observations:<br> 0  1  3  4  8 10 14 25 <br>24  1  1  1  2  1  1  1 </font></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span><br></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span><font size=\"1\">&gt;summary(model$</font>\r\n<font size=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span><span>ab_140_det_0.1725)</span></span></span></span></span></font></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span><font size=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal\"><span><span><span><span>Call:<br>gmultmix(lambdaformula = ~1, phiformula = ~1, pformula = ~1, <br>    data = x, mixture = &quot;P&quot;, method = &quot;Nelder-Mead&quot;, se = T)<br><br>Abundance (log-scale):<br> Estimate    SE    z   P(&gt;|z|)<br>     4.29 0.117 36.7 3.21e-294<br><br>Detection (logit-scale):<br> Estimate    SE     z  P(&gt;|z|)<br>   -0.658 0.144 -4.57 4.98e-06<br><br>AIC: -201.7269 <br>Number of sites: 1<br>optim convergence code: 0<br>optim iterations: 79 <br>Bootstrap iterations: 0</span></span></span></span></span></font></span></span></span></span></div><div><span style=